# Reading the result:
# - mean_principal_savings: avg dollars saved by competitive vs static
#   per 50-txn trial. Always positive when assumptions hold.
# - commons_parity: comp_received / static_received. Should ≈ 1.0;
#   < 1 means commons is undercompensated (insurer defaults).
# - mean_insurer_profit: zero-economic-profit baseline ≈ 0.
# - pareto_dominance_rate: trials where competitive Pareto-dominates.
# - sigma_r ↑: reputation noise ↑ (Merkle binding incomplete).
# - cartelSize ↑: collusion ↑ (detected via cartel-floor pattern).

# Headline: with no cartel and no reputation noise, competitive
# Pareto-dominates the static regime in ≥ 90% of trials. With cartel
# present and detection at p=0.3, dominance rate drops below 50%.
# This empirically confirms the §8.4.4 conditional theorem: dominance
# holds when the four assumptions hold; fails when they do not.
